    <!-- ══ STRATEGIC VISION ══ -->
    <section class="section" id="vision">
      <div class="section-kicker">Why We're Doing This</div>
      <h2>Strategic Vision</h2>
      <hr class="section-rule">

      <p class="section-intro">The FCIP product team spends significant time on ceremonies, documentation, and communications that are structurally repetitive — but currently require expert domain knowledge to execute well. This creates a bottleneck: the people who understand financial crime deeply are the ones manually writing Jira tickets, Confluence pages, and release comms. The goal is to recover that capacity for high-value investigation work, while maintaining — and ultimately improving — the quality and compliance rigour of every artefact the team produces.</p>

      <div class="info-box">
        <strong>Design Principle</strong>
        Every agentic capability must preserve human decision authority on anything touching regulatory obligations. The agent drafts, recommends, and automates — a qualified human approves, submits, and signs off. This is not optional: it is a regulatory requirement under POCA 2002, MLRs 2017, and FCA SYSC.
      </div>

      <div class="info-box">
        <strong>Starting Point</strong>
        Today's prompt bank (Phase 1) is not a compromise — it is a deliberate strategy. By encoding domain knowledge into structured prompts first, the team builds the prompt library and tests prompt quality in a low-risk environment. Every Phase 2, 3, and 4 capability builds directly on the prompts already proven in Phase 1.
      </div>

      <p class="section-intro" style="margin-bottom:0">The end state is a product operations agent that can receive a goal statement — "we need to enable DAML consent SAR submission from FCIP" — and autonomously produce a Jira epic, child stories meeting Definition of Ready, a Confluence design page, compliance risk flags, and an NFR checklist. A senior team member reviews the output in 20 minutes rather than producing it over 3 days.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ ARCHITECTURE ══ -->
    <section class="section" id="architecture">
      <div class="section-kicker">Technical Blueprint</div>
      <h2>Target Architecture</h2>
      <hr class="section-rule">

      <p class="section-intro">The agentic system sits outside the FCIP application itself — it is a product operations layer, not a feature of the investigation platform. It reads from and writes to Jira and Confluence via MCP servers, using the LLM as an orchestration engine grounded by the Financial Crime Context file.</p>

      <div class="arch-diagram">
        <div class="arch-title">FCIP AGENTIC PRODUCT OPS — SYSTEM LAYERS</div>
        <div class="arch-layers">

          <div class="arch-layer">
            <div class="arch-layer-label">Human Layer</div>
            <div class="arch-layer-boxes">
              <div class="arch-box human">Product Director</div>
              <div class="arch-box human">Product Owner</div>
              <div class="arch-box human">Compliance Reviewer</div>
              <div class="arch-box human">Tech Lead</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="arch-connector">↕ goal input / review &amp; approve output</div>

          <div class="arch-layer">
            <div class="arch-layer-label">Agent Layer</div>
            <div class="arch-layer-boxes">
              <div class="arch-box agent">Orchestrator Agent</div>
              <div class="arch-box agent">Epic Writer Sub-Agent</div>
              <div class="arch-box agent">Story Decomposer Sub-Agent</div>
              <div class="arch-box agent">Docs Generator Sub-Agent</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="arch-connector">↕ tool calls via MCP</div>

          <div class="arch-layer">
            <div class="arch-layer-label">Tool Layer</div>
            <div class="arch-layer-boxes">
              <div class="arch-box tool">Jira MCP (read/write)</div>
              <div class="arch-box tool">Confluence MCP (read/write)</div>
              <div class="arch-box tool">Web Search</div>
              <div class="arch-box tool">Regulatory Lookup</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="arch-connector">↕ read / write</div>

          <div class="arch-layer">
            <div class="arch-layer-label">Data Layer</div>
            <div class="arch-layer-boxes">
              <div class="arch-box data">Jira Project (FCIP)</div>
              <div class="arch-box data">Confluence Space</div>
              <div class="arch-box data">FC Context File (ground truth)</div>
              <div class="arch-box data">Prompt Bank</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="arch-connector">↕ embedded in every agent call</div>

          <div class="arch-layer">
            <div class="arch-layer-label">Guardrails</div>
            <div class="arch-layer-boxes">
              <div class="arch-box guard">Human Approval Gate</div>
