      <div class="warn-box">
        <strong>Bank Security Requirement</strong>
        Any agentic integration with Jira or Confluence must go through the bank's AI governance review process and receive CISO sign-off before production use. Credentials for MCP server connections must be managed through the approved secrets management toolchain — never hardcoded or held in prompts.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ AGENTIC WORKFLOW ══ -->
    <section class="section" id="flow">
      <div class="section-kicker">How It Works</div>
      <h2>Agentic Workflow</h2>
      <hr class="section-rule">

      <p class="section-intro">In the fully agentic state (Phase 4), a single goal statement triggers an orchestrated sequence of sub-agent tasks, each grounded by the FC Context file and each producing output that feeds the next step. The human touch-points are deliberate checkpoints, not bottlenecks.</p>

      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-icon">🎯</div>
          <div class="flow-title">Goal Input</div>
          <div class="flow-desc">Director inputs a product goal in natural language. Agent requests any missing context.</div>
          <div class="flow-phase" style="background:rgba(45,106,79,0.12);color:var(--p1)">P1 today</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-icon">📋</div>
          <div class="flow-title">Epic Draft</div>
          <div class="flow-desc">Agent generates structured epic with compliance flags, scope boundary, and success metrics.</div>
          <div class="flow-phase" style="background:rgba(45,106,79,0.12);color:var(--p1)">P1 today</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-icon">✅</div>
          <div class="flow-title">Human Review</div>
          <div class="flow-desc">PO reviews epic. Approves, edits, or rejects. Agent incorporates feedback.</div>
          <div class="flow-phase" style="background:rgba(26,92,138,0.12);color:var(--p2)">Always required</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-icon">📝</div>
          <div class="flow-title">Story Decomposition</div>
          <div class="flow-desc">Agent breaks epic into stories, runs DoR check, writes Gherkin ACs for each.</div>
          <div class="flow-phase" style="background:rgba(45,106,79,0.12);color:var(--p1)">P1 today</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-icon">🔗</div>
          <div class="flow-title">Jira Write-Back</div>
          <div class="flow-desc">Agent creates epic and child stories in Jira via MCP. Links NFRs and compliance flags.</div>
          <div class="flow-phase" style="background:rgba(107,45,107,0.12);color:var(--p4)">Phase 4</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="flow-icon">📄</div>
          <div class="flow-title">Confluence Docs</div>
          <div class="flow-desc">Agent publishes training pack, NFR page, and design rationale to Confluence automatically.</div>
          <div class="flow-phase" style="background:rgba(107,45,107,0.12);color:var(--p4)">Phase 4</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="info-box">
        <strong>Key Design Choice: Human-in-the-Loop at Every Write</strong>
        Even in Phase 4, the agent never writes to Jira or Confluence without a human confirmation step. The agent proposes; a team member approves. This is both a governance requirement and a quality mechanism — the agent may generate 90% of the content but the domain expert provides the final 10% that makes it correct and contextually appropriate.
      </div>
    </section>

