      <p class="section-intro">Model Context Protocol (MCP) is the standard that allows LLM agents to call external tools and services. The three MCP integrations below are required for Phase 3 and 4. Each has a distinct data governance profile that must be reviewed before enabling.</p>

      <div class="mcp-grid">
        <div class="mcp-card">
          <div class="mcp-icon">🗂️</div>
          <div class="mcp-name">Jira MCP</div>
          <div class="mcp-url">atlassian.com MCP server</div>
          <div class="mcp-desc">Enables the agent to read epics, stories, sprint data, and backlog items live. Phase 4 adds write capability to create and update tickets. Requires OAuth app registration in the bank's Atlassian instance.</div>
          <div class="mcp-phase" style="background:rgba(123,94,42,0.12);color:var(--p3)">Phase 3: Read · Phase 4: Write</div>
        </div>

        <div class="mcp-card">
          <div class="mcp-icon">📚</div>
          <div class="mcp-name">Confluence MCP</div>
          <div class="mcp-url">atlassian.com MCP server</div>
          <div class="mcp-desc">Allows the agent to read existing design docs, ADRs, and runbooks for context, then publish new pages for training packs, NFR specs, and release notes. Requires space-level permissions scoping.</div>
          <div class="mcp-phase" style="background:rgba(123,94,42,0.12);color:var(--p3)">Phase 3: Read · Phase 4: Write</div>
        </div>

        <div class="mcp-card">
          <div class="mcp-icon">🔍</div>
          <div class="mcp-name">Web Search MCP</div>
          <div class="mcp-url">search tool (Anthropic native)</div>
          <div class="mcp-desc">Allows the agent to look up current regulatory guidance — e.g. latest NCA SAR reporting thresholds, FATF typology updates, or FCA Dear CEO letters — and incorporate them into outputs without manual research.</div>
          <div class="mcp-phase" style="background:rgba(26,92,138,0.12);color:var(--p2)">Phase 2 onwards</div>
        </div>

        <div class="mcp-card">
          <div class="mcp-icon">📧</div>
          <div class="mcp-name">Gmail / Outlook MCP</div>
